Sebastian Hungerecker <sepp00@web.de> writes:
> [ dipping unwanted +?! for later re-use ]
> If you have water walking or magical breathing and a pick-axe you
> can turn the fountain into a pool and use it for #dipping without
> the chance of getting nasties.

I routinely make pools this way and use them, without unbreathing,
water-walking or similar. AFAIK, it's safe provided that:

1) There is at least one square of regular floor next to your pool,
2) You are not burdened (or worse), and
3) There is nothing in your inventory subject to water damage (other
   than the stuff you _want_ soaked), and
4) You don't drown your pet.

You can't #dip (as you don't stay in the water), but each item in your
backpack has a chance of getting wet. Just keep diving in until all ?+
are blanked and all ! are water.

Am I courting death here without realizing it? (A quick venture into
trap.c suggests it is categorically safe, not just probabilistically
so.)

